Two applications are running in different VPCs and need secure communication. How would you design the connectivity?



1.VPC Peering connects two VPCs using the cloud providers internal, private backbone network. Traffic remains entirely private and never traverses the public internet.

2.AWS PrivateLink is the ideal solution for Application B acts strictly as a "service" or API provider to Application A—or if both VPCs have overlapping IP address blocks

3.If we require strict, fine-grained HTTP/HTTPS request-level authentication without managing complex routing tables, Amazon VPC Lattice provides a managed service mesh layer.



